{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-job-16-1","title":"Job 16:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Job reproves his friends for unmercifulness. 17 He maintains his innocency.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-2","title":"Job 16:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>heard. 6:6,25; 11:2,3; 13:5; 19:2,3; 26:2,3; Jas 1:19 miserable. or, troublesome. 13:4; Ps 69:26; Php 1:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-3","title":"Job 16:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>vain words. Heb. words of wind. 6:26; 8:2; 15:2 what emboldeneth. 20:3; 32:3-6; Mt 22:46; Tit 1:11; 2:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-4","title":"Job 16:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>if your soul. 6:2-5,14; Mt 7:12; Ro 12:15; 1Co 12:26 up words. 11:2; 35:16; Pr 10:19; Ec 10:14 shake mine. 2Ki 19:21; Ps 22:7; 44:14; 109:25; Jer 18:16; La 2:15; Mt 27:39,40</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-5","title":"Job 16:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>But I would. 4:3,4; 6:14; 29:25; Ps 27:14; Pr 27:9,17; Isa 35:3,4; Ga 6:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-6","title":"Job 16:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>my grief. 10:1; Ps 77:1-9; 88:15-18 what am I eased. Heb. what goeth from me.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-7","title":"Job 16:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>he hath. 3:17; 7:3,16; 10:1; Ps 6:6,7; Pr 3:11,12; Isa 50:4; Mic 6:13 hast made. 1:15-19; 29:5-25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-8","title":"Job 16:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>And thou hast, etc.Some render, \"thou has fettered me,\" as {kamat} signifies in Arabic; but as it signifies in Syriac to be wrinkled, the common version seems, from the connexion, to be more correct; and if Job's disease were the elephantiasis, these words would apply most forcibly to the wrinkled state of the skin in that disorder.</p>\n<p>is a witness. 10:17; Ru 1:21; Eph 5:27 my leanness. Ps 106:15; Isa 10:16; 24:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-9","title":"Job 16:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>teareth me. 10:16,17; 18:4; Ps 50:22; La 3:10; Ho 5:14 he gnasheth. Ps 35:16; 37:12; La 2:16 mine. 13:24,27; 19:11; Mic 7:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-10","title":"Job 16:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>gaped. Ps 22:13,16,17; 35:21; Lu 23:35,36 they have smitten. 1Ki 22:24; 2Ch 18:23; Isa 50:6; La 3:30; Mic 5:1; Mt 26:67 Joh 18:22; Ac 23:2; 2Co 11:20 gathered. Ps 35:15; 94:21; Ac 4:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-11","title":"Job 16:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>delivered me. Heb. shut me up. 1Sa 24:18; *marg: Ps 31:8; Ro 11:32; *marg: to the ungodly. 1:13-19; 2:7; Ps 7:14; Joh 19:16; 2Co 12:7 turned. Ps 27:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-12","title":"Job 16:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>at ease. 1:2,3; 3:26; 29:3,18,19 broken me. 4:10; Ps 44:19; La 3:4; Mt 21:44 by my neck. 15:26; Ro 16:4 shaken. La 3:11; Eze 29:7 set me up. 7:12,20; La 3:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-13","title":"Job 16:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>archers. 6:4; Ge 49:23; Ps 7:12,13 he cleaveth. 19:27; La 3:13 doth. 6:10; De 29:20; Eze 5:11; Ro 8:32; 2Pe 2:5 poureth. 20:25; La 2:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-14","title":"Job 16:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>breaketh. La 3:3-5 runneth. Jud 15:8; Ps 42:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-15","title":"Job 16:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>sewed. 1Ki 21:27; Isa 22:12 defiled my horn. 30:19; 1Sa 2:10; Ps 7:5; 75:5,10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-16","title":"Job 16:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>face. Ps 6:6,7; 31:9; 32:3; 69:3; 102:3-5,9; Isa 52:14; La 1:16 on my eyelids. 17:7; Ps 116:3; Jon 2:1-10; Mr 14:34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-17","title":"Job 16:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>Not for. 11:14; 15:20,34; 21:27,28; 22:5-9; 27:6,7; 29:12-17; 31:1-40 Ps 7:3-5; 44:17-21 my prayer. 8:5,6; Ps 66:18,19; Pr 15:8; 1Ti 2:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-18","title":"Job 16:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>O earth. Jer 22:29 cover not. Ge 4:11; Ne 4:5; Isa 26:21; Eze 24:7 let my cry. 27:9; Ps 66:18,19; Isa 1:15; 58:9,10; Jas 4:3,4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-19","title":"Job 16:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>my witness. 1Sa 12:5; Ro 1:9; 9:1; 2Co 1:23; 11:31; 1Th 2:10 on high. Heb. in the high places. 25:2; Ps 113:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-20","title":"Job 16:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>scorn me. Heb. are my scorners. 4; 12:4,5; 17:2 poureth. Ps 109:4; 142:2; Ho 12:4,5; Lu 6:11,12; Heb 5:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-21","title":"Job 16:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>plead. 9:34,35; 13:3,22; 23:3-7; 31:35; 40:1-5; Ec 6:10; Isa 45:9; Ro 9:20 neighbour. or, friend.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-16-22","title":"Job 16:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>a few years. Heb. years of number. 14:5,14 whence. 7:9,10; 14:10; Ec 12:5</p>"}]}